<title>UK: Turkey prices five-year bond, ups to $300 million.</title>
<headline>Turkey prices five-year bond, ups to $300 million.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following, announced earlier by joint lead managers J.P. Morgan Securities and SBC Warburg, has been priced and increased by $50 million.</p>
<p> BORROWER   TURKEY</p>
<p> AMT	  $300 MLN  COUPON     10.00     MATURITY    23.MAY.02</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  99.923    PAY DATE    23.MAY.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  =	   REOFFER    99.923    SPREAD	+350 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	B1	  LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  B	   DENOMS (K) 10	  SALE LIMITS =</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.00	HOME CTRY  TURKEY    TAX PROVS   =</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 6.625 PCT U.S. TREASURY NOTE DUE 30.APR.02</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 8863</p>
